# Listing, Release Notes & User Feedback

- `LISTING.md` is the source of truth for the AMO product page (summary + full description). Whenever a user-facing feature is added, changed, or removed, update `LISTING.md` in the same change, so the live AMO page never falls out of sync with what the extension actually does.
- Every user-facing change gets an entry in `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` at the time it's made — not retroactively before a release.
- Before any listed release (`release-prod` skill), move the `[Unreleased]` entries into a new version section in `CHANGELOG.md`, and copy that section's text into `amo-metadata.json` → `version.release_notes.en-US`. A listed version must never ship with empty or stale release notes.
- Only document **user-visible** behavior in `CHANGELOG.md`/release notes — skip internal refactors, CI/tooling changes, and test-only work unless they affect what the user experiences.
- After a listed release goes live, check AMO Ratings & Reviews and reply to critical reviews (see `LISTING.md` → User feedback loop). Real bugs reported in reviews go into `ROADMAP.md` before replying.
